</style></head><body><a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to report</a><header><h1 id="report-title">A0 rectangular-wall compressional Alfvén benchmark</h1><p class="prose">Independent cold Hall reference and accepted nonlinear RK4 trajectories in the grid-aligned RZ conductor box. The final evidence includes fixed-box refinement, half-step timing, matched quiet drift and a physical wall-distance control.</p></header><main id="main"><section id="notation"><h2>Notation</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Symbol</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>R, Z</td><td>Physical poloidal cross-section coordinates in m</td></tr><tr><td>n_phi, K</td><td>Toroidal harmonic index and retained Fourier cutoff</td></tr><tr><td>δB_parallel</td><td>Toroidal magnetic perturbation parallel to the vacuum guide field</td></tr></tbody></table></section><section id="archive"><h2>Archive</h2><a href="MODE_REPORT.md">Methods, metrics and run links</a></section><nav id="report-index" aria-label="Report pages"><h2>Report pages</h2><ol><li><a href="#page-reference">Cold Hall short control</a></li><li><a href="#page-mode">Tracked n_phi=1 mode</a></li><li><a href="#page-physical-fields">Absolute physical fields and matched differences</a></li><li><a href="#page-controls">Separate mesh, time-step and wall controls</a></li><li><a href="#page-physical-resolution">Physical spatial resolution</a></li></ol></nav></main><article class="report-page" id="page-reference"><p class="page-counter">Page 1 / 5</p><nav class="page-nav" aria-label="Page navigation"><a href="#report-index">Index</a><a href="#report-index">Previous</a><a href="#page-mode">Next</a></nav><h2>Cold Hall short control</h2><p class="prose">A previously defined exact axial standing wave checks the repaired spatial path before the toroidal mode comparison.</p><figure id="figure-1"><h3>Figure 1: Axial wave phase and span error</h3><img src="cold-hall-control.png" alt="Axial wave phase and span error"><figcaption><span class="source-badge mixed">MIX | explicit components: accepted A0 evolution; independent cold Hall reference</span><span class="figure-caption">The 12 ns accepted trajectory is compared to the independently given wave at each saved time.</span><dl class="figure-metadata"><dt>N_R</dt><dd>8</dd><dt>N_Z</dt><dd>8</dd><dt>n_phi (toroidal harmonic)</dt><dd>0</dd></dl><p class="artifact-links">Files: <a href="cold-hall-short-comparison.json">DATA</a> </p></figcaption></figure></article><article class="report-page" id="page-mode"><p class="page-counter">Page 2 / 5</p><nav class="page-nav" aria-label="Page navigation"><a href="#report-index">Index</a><a href="#page-reference">Previous</a><a href="#page-physical-fields">Next</a></nav><h2>Tracked n_phi=1 mode</h2><p class="prose">The modal phase is fitted from accepted state outputs. The independent reference and the local frozen source are recorded separately.</p><figure id="figure-2"><h3>Figure 2: 16×16 accepted frequency and phase</h3><img src="analysis-r15-g16/phase-amplitude.png" alt="16×16 accepted frequency and phase"><figcaption><span class="source-badge mixed">MIX | explicit components: accepted A0 evolution; independent cold Hall reference</span><span class="figure-caption">Fitted frequency 5.648532 MHz and independent value 6.176967 MHz.</span><dl class="figure-metadata"><dt>N_R</dt><dd>16</dd><dt>N_Z</dt><dd>16</dd><dt>n_phi (toroidal harmonic)</dt><dd>1</dd><dt>Device</dt><dd>RTX 5090</dd></dl><p class="artifact-links">Files: <a href="analysis-r15-g16/mode-data.npz">DATA</a> </p></figcaption></figure><figure id="figure-3"><h3>Figure 3: Parallel magnetic field structure</h3><img src="analysis-r15-g16/mode-structure.png" alt="Parallel magnetic field structure"><figcaption><span class="source-badge mixed">MIX | explicit components: accepted A0 evolution; independent cold Hall reference</span><span class="figure-caption">Full-box overlap 0.764 and overlap 0.952 at ≥0.20 m from the wall. Separate RMS normalization makes the comparison a shape diagnostic.</span><dl class="figure-metadata"><dt>N_R</dt><dd>16</dd><dt>N_Z</dt><dd>16</dd><dt>n_phi (toroidal harmonic)</dt><dd>1</dd><dt>Device</dt><dd>RTX 5090</dd></dl><p class="artifact-links">Files: <a href="analysis-r15-g16/mode-data.npz">DATA</a> </p></figcaption></figure><details class="figure-details"><summary>Figure 4: Magnetic polarization - MIX | explicit components</summary><figure id="figure-4"><h3>Figure 4: Magnetic polarization</h3><img src="analysis-r15-g16/polarization.png" alt="Magnetic polarization"><figcaption><span class="source-badge mixed">MIX | explicit components: accepted A0 evolution; independent cold Hall reference</span><span class="figure-caption">The magnetic components use the same phase and one parallel-field normalization. Colorbars are separate by component.</span><dl class="figure-metadata"><dt>N_R</dt><dd>16</dd><dt>N_Z</dt><dd>16</dd><dt>n_phi (toroidal harmonic)</dt><dd>1</dd></dl><p class="artifact-links">Files: <a href="analysis-r15-g16/mode-data.npz">DATA</a> </p></figcaption></figure></details></article><article class="report-page" id="page-physical-fields"><p class="page-counter">Page 3 / 5</p><nav class="page-nav" aria-label="Page navigation"><a href="#report-index">Index</a><a href="#page-mode">Previous</a><a href="#page-controls">Next</a></nav><h2>Absolute physical fields and matched differences</h2><p class="prose">The first two columns show the full field in the quiet and perturbed runs at the same physical time. The right column uses the difference at that time.</p><figure id="figure-5"><h3>Figure 5: 16×16 physical RZ sections</h3><img src="analysis-r15-g16/total-fields.png" alt="16×16 physical RZ sections"><figcaption><span class="source-badge nl">NL | FOMHD time evolution</span><span class="figure-caption">Ion density, magnetic magnitude, ion speed and electric magnitude at φ=0. The full density color scale starts at zero. Black lines denote the conducting walls.</span><dl class="figure-metadata"><dt>N_R</dt><dd>16</dd><dt>N_Z</dt><dd>16</dd><dt>n_phi (toroidal harmonic)</dt><dd>1</dd></dl><p class="artifact-links">Files: <a href="analysis-r15-g16/matched-physical-fields.npz">DATA</a> </p></figcaption></figure><details class="figure-details"><summary>Figure 6: 16×16 pressures before and after subtraction - NL | FOMHD time evolution</summary><figure id="figure-6"><h3>Figure 6: 16×16 pressures before and after subtraction</h3><img src="analysis-r15-g16/total-pressure.png" alt="16×16 pressures before and after subtraction"><figcaption><span class="source-badge nl">NL | FOMHD time evolution</span><span class="figure-caption">The scalar ion pressure and both electron pressure components are shown in physical units.</span><dl class="figure-metadata"><dt>N_R</dt><dd>16</dd><dt>N_Z</dt><dd>16</dd><dt>n_phi (toroidal harmonic)</dt><dd>1</dd></dl><p class="artifact-links">Files: <a href="analysis-r15-g16/matched-physical-fields.npz">DATA</a> </p></figcaption></figure></details></article><article class="report-page" id="page-controls"><p class="page-counter">Page 4 / 5</p><nav class="page-nav" aria-label="Page navigation"><a href="#report-index">Index</a><a href="#page-physical-fields">Previous</a><a href="#page-physical-resolution">Next</a></nav><h2>Separate mesh, time-step and wall controls</h2><p class="prose">The mesh series holds the physical walls fixed. The wall series holds the cell spacing and the time step fixed.</p><figure id="figure-7"><h3>Figure 7: Separate physical and numerical sensitivities</h3><img src="refinement-time-wall-controls.png" alt="Separate physical and numerical sensitivities"><figcaption><span class="source-badge mixed">MIX | explicit components: accepted A0 evolution; independent cold Hall reference</span><span class="figure-caption">Fixed-domain grid refinement, matched half-step phase gap and same-spacing physical wall movement.</span><p class="artifact-links">Files: <a href="control-comparison.json">DATA</a> </p></figcaption></figure><figure id="figure-8"><h3>Figure 8: Wider physical wall structure</h3><img src="analysis-r15-wide/mode-structure.png" alt="Wider physical wall structure"><figcaption><span class="source-badge mixed">MIX | explicit components: accepted A0 evolution; independent cold Hall reference</span><span class="figure-caption">The wider box uses the same 0.075 m cells as the narrow 16×16 case.</span><dl class="figure-metadata"><dt>N_R</dt><dd>20</dd><dt>N_Z</dt><dd>20</dd><dt>n_phi (toroidal harmonic)</dt><dd>1</dd></dl><p class="artifact-links">Files: <a href="analysis-r15-wide/mode-data.npz">DATA</a> </p></figcaption></figure><details class="figure-details"><summary>Figure 9: Wider-box absolute RZ sections - NL | FOMHD time evolution</summary><figure id="figure-9"><h3>Figure 9: Wider-box absolute RZ sections</h3><img src="analysis-r15-wide/total-fields.png" alt="Wider-box absolute RZ sections"><figcaption><span class="source-badge nl">NL | FOMHD time evolution</span><span class="figure-caption">The accepted perturbed state and the analytic static background share an absolute color scale. The difference column subtracts that static background. Black frames denote the outward-shifted conducting walls.</span><dl class="figure-metadata"><dt>N_R</dt><dd>20</dd><dt>N_Z</dt><dd>20</dd><dt>n_phi (toroidal harmonic)</dt><dd>1</dd></dl><p class="artifact-links">Files: <a href="analysis-r15-wide/accepted-total-and-background.npz">DATA</a> </p></figcaption></figure></details><figure id="figure-10"><h3>Figure 10: Physical structures across the three meshes</h3><img src="refinement-structure.png" alt="Physical structures across the three meshes"><figcaption><span class="source-badge mixed">MIX | explicit components: accepted A0 evolution; independent cold Hall reference</span><span class="figure-caption">Fixed-box grids are shown beside the wider physical box. Dotted lines identify the fixed 0.20 m wall collar, and all panels share one normalized scale.</span><p class="artifact-links">Files: <a href="control-comparison.json">DATA</a> </p></figcaption></figure></article><article class="report-page" id="page-physical-resolution"><p class="page-counter">Page 5 / 5</p><nav class="page-nav" aria-label="Page navigation"><a href="#report-index">Index</a><a href="#page-controls">Previous</a><a href="#report-index">Next</a></nav><h2>Physical spatial resolution</h2><p class="prose">The continuous reference supplies the directional wavelengths and dominant lobe widths. The fixed-box grid and time estimates are kept separate from the wider physical box.</p><figure id="figure-11"><h3>Figure 11: Independent mode scales and cuts</h3><img src="ritz-spatial-scales.png" alt="Independent mode scales and cuts"><figcaption><span class="source-badge ref">REF | independent model</span><span class="figure-caption">The cuts mark the connected amplitude half-maximum intervals in R and Z. Grid counts and the next fixed-box measurement are recorded in the methods.</span><dl class="figure-metadata"><dt>n_phi (toroidal harmonic)</dt><dd>1</dd></dl><p class="artifact-links">Files: <a href="ritz-spatial-scales.json">DATA</a> </p></figcaption></figure></article><section id="conclusions"><h2>Conclusions</h2><p class="prose">A0 follows the independently identified compressional branch over four measured periods and resolves the dominant interior structure. The full-box near-wall shape and absolute frequency retain measurable discrepancies at this resolution.</p><h3>Known issues</h3><ul><li><a href="independent-review/REVIEW.md">Independent branch screening and full-domain near-wall limits</a></li></ul></section><footer>Supplied figures support review but do not by themselves establish convergence or scientific acceptance.</footer></body></html>
